WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:10.962
Hi! When we go shopping or save money in a bank, we use percentages. Today we'll learn about discount, GST and interest.

2
00:00:11.112 --> 00:00:18.162
At the garden shop, a watering can usually costs 50 dollars. Now there's a 20 percent discount.

3
00:00:18.312 --> 00:00:24.834
The discount is 20 percent of the usual price. 20 percent of 50 is 10 dollars.

4
00:00:24.984 --> 00:00:30.354
So we pay 50 minus 10, which is 40 dollars.

5
00:00:30.504 --> 00:00:40.122
GST is the Goods and Services Tax. It is added on top of the price. In Singapore, the GST rate is now 9 percent.

6
00:00:40.272 --> 00:00:49.290
A lawn mower costs 200 dollars before GST. The GST is 9 percent of 200, which is 18 dollars.

7
00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:55.314
So altogether we pay 200 plus 18, which is 218 dollars.

8
00:00:55.464 --> 00:01:02.178
In a question, you will be told the rate. Always use the rate the question gives.

9
00:01:02.328 --> 00:01:08.154
We save 1000 dollars in a bank. The annual interest rate is 2 percent.

10
00:01:08.304 --> 00:01:14.514
After one year, the bank pays interest of 2 percent of 1000, which is 20 dollars.

11
00:01:14.664 --> 00:01:22.002
So after one year, we have 1000 plus 20, which is 1020 dollars.

12
00:01:22.152 --> 00:01:29.202
One more: a bag costs 80 dollars, with a 15 percent discount. How much do we pay?

13
00:01:29.352 --> 00:01:37.938
The discount is 15 percent of 80. 10 percent is 8 dollars, and 5 percent is 4 dollars, so it's 12 dollars.

14
00:01:38.088 --> 00:01:43.578
We pay 80 minus 12, which is 68 dollars.

15
00:01:43.728 --> 00:01:52.074
Watch out! Some pupils see a 20 percent discount and do 50 minus 20 to get 30 dollars. That is wrong!

16
00:01:52.224 --> 00:01:59.514
20 percent means 20 percent of 50 dollars, which is 10 dollars. So we pay 40 dollars.

17
00:01:59.664 --> 00:02:07.626
Discount, GST and interest are all a percentage of the original amount. Work that out first.

18
00:02:07.776 --> 00:02:20.298
Your turn! An item costs 300 dollars before 9 percent GST. How much do we pay altogether? Pause and think.

19
00:02:20.448 --> 00:02:30.762
The GST is 27 dollars. 300 plus 27 is 327 dollars. Did you get it right?

20
00:02:30.912 --> 00:02:44.226
Another one! We save 1500 dollars at 3 percent interest per year. How much interest do we get after one year? Pause and think.

21
00:02:44.376 --> 00:02:51.666
3 percent of 1500 is 45 dollars. Did you get it right?

22
00:02:51.816 --> 00:03:00.210
Remember: first find the percentage of the original amount. Subtract a discount. Add GST and interest.

23
00:03:00.360 --> 00:03:04.554
Now go and practise in your garden!

